#: 4.x/index.html
msgid "<h1 id=i-classfas-fa-utensilsinbspgodot-recipes><i class='fas fa-utensils'></i> Godot Recipes</h1><blockquote><p>Godot&rsquo;s nodes are your ingredients. What can you cook up?</p></blockquote><p>On this site you&rsquo;ll find a collection of solutions and examples to help you make whatever game system you need.</p><div class=\"box notices cstyle tip\"><div class=box-label><i class=\"fa-fw fas fa-lightbulb\"></i> Godot 4.0</div><div class=box-content><p><strong>Godot 4.0 has been released!</strong><br>Godot 4.0 is the latest stable release version of the engine.<br>This site also has lots of learning material for Godot 3 - much of it is still useful! You can click the ribbon in the top-right to toggle the Godot Recipes version, or click the button below:<br></p><span class=\"btn cstyle primary\"><a href=/godot_recipes/3.x/><i class=\"fa-fw fas fa-utensils\"></i> Godot 3 Recipes</a></span></div></div><p>Are you ready to learn game development? Whether it&rsquo;s as a hobby or working towards your dream career, there&rsquo;s never been a better time to get started. Modern programming languages and tools have made it easier than ever to build high-quality games and distribute them to the world. One of these tools is the Godot game engine. For beginners, it offers a friendly way to learn gamedev techniques. For experienced developers, it&rsquo;s a powerful, customizable and <em>open</em> tool for bringing your visions to life.</p><p><a href=#image-e722c27caf3da1c62cf6c099ec530b76 class=lightbox-link><img src=\"/godot_recipes/4.x/img/godot3_logo.png?width=400px\" alt=alt style=height:auto;width:400px loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-e722c27caf3da1c62cf6c099ec530b76><img src=\"/godot_recipes/4.x/img/godot3_logo.png?width=400px\" alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><p>On this site you&rsquo;ll find a gentle introduction to the Godot game engine, as well as a wide variety of gamedev tips and techniques. Feel free to browse the categories in the sidebar and see what catches your interest.</p><p>If you&rsquo;re new to Godot, start here: <a href=/godot_recipes/4.x/g101/start/101_01/>What is Godot?</a>.</p><h3 id=how-to-use-this-site>How to use this site</h3><h4 id=beginners>Beginners</h4><p>If you&rsquo;re new to game development, start with the <a href=/godot_recipes/4.x/basics/>&ldquo;Godot 101: Basics&rdquo;</a> section. There you&rsquo;ll find an introduction to the Godot application, and a step-by-step guide to creating your first project. There is a lot of material to absorb here. Don&rsquo;t feel discouraged if you feel you don&rsquo;t get it at first. Repetition is the key to learning complex topics; the more you work with Godot&rsquo;s features, the more familiar and <em>easy</em> they will start to feel.</p><div class=\"box notices cstyle info\"><div class=box-label><i class=\"fa-fw fas fa-info-circle\"></i> Info</div><div class=box-content><p>It&rsquo;s assumed that you have at least some general programming experience. If you&rsquo;re <em>completely</em> new to programming, click <a href=https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/getting_started/step_by_step/index.html target=_blank>here</a> for tips on how to get started.</p></div></div><h4 id=experienced-developers>Experienced Developers</h4><p>If you&rsquo;re an experienced developer and/or you&rsquo;re familiar with other modern game engine(s), feel free to explore the menu on the left. You&rsquo;ll find a number of useful guides and tutorials to show you how to do things the &ldquo;Godot Way&rdquo;. Code samples and example projects are available for all articles.</p><footer class=footline></footer>"
msgstr ""

