msgid "<h1 id=radial-popup-menu>Radial Popup Menu</h1><h2 id=problem>Problem</h2><p>You want a radial menu - a ring of buttons that pops up for you to choose an option.</p><h2 id=solution>Solution</h2><p>Radial menus are used in a variety of games to allow access to a selection of buttons. For example, clicking on an NPC in a game allows you to choose what action to take: talk, inspect, attack, etc.</p><p>The specific look-and-feel of your menu should match with your game&rsquo;s esthetic. For this demo, we&rsquo;ll focus on the mechanics of making the menu work, and leave the styling choices to you.</p><p>Here&rsquo;s the node setup:</p><p><a href=#image-5f59051cd0f53e6bdaec4302f41d07cf class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/ui_radial_menu_01_4.png alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-5f59051cd0f53e6bdaec4302f41d07cf><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/ui_radial_menu_01_4.png alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><p>We&rsquo;re using a <i class=gd-TextureButton></i> as our root node. This is the button you&rsquo;ll click to open/close the menu.</p><p>The <i class=gd-Control></i> node is the container where you&rsquo;ll place any number of items that you want. Make sure to set this control&rsquo;s <strong>Mouse/Filter</strong> property to &ldquo;Ignore&rdquo; so that it won&rsquo;t intercept mouse clicks.</p><p>For this example, we&rsquo;re using 9 buttons from our <a href=/godot_recipes/4.x/ui/cooldown_button/>Cooldown Button</a> recipe.</p><p>Now, let&rsquo;s look at the script for the button:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Here are our variables. represents the &ldquo;size&rdquo; of the menu: the radius of the circle. is for the animation - smaller numbers are faster.</p><p> keeps track of how many buttons there are, while is a flag to track whether the menu is open or closed.</p><div class=highlight></div><p>In we start setting things up: hiding the menu buttons by default, and setting their positions to that of the main button.</p><p>Now connect the signal of the main button.</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Clicking the button shows/hides the menu. We also need to disable the button, or else clicking again <em>while</em> the tween is playing would restart it.</p><div class=highlight></div><p>When the tween animation finishes, toggle the active state and enable the button again.</p><p>Let&rsquo;s look at the function:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>In this function we calculate the angle we need between each item (). We then loop through each button and find its destination () based on this angle and the chosen . For each button, we&rsquo;re tweening two properties, and , to get our desired effect.</p><p> performs the exact opposite function:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Here&rsquo;s the end result:</p><p><a href=#image-879d806e30bb36ecb93939ee78147e05 class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/ui_radial_menu_02.gif alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-879d806e30bb36ecb93939ee78147e05><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/ui_radial_menu_02.gif alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><h2 id=i-classfas-fa-code-branchi-download-this-project><i class=\"fas fa-code-branch\"></i> Download This Project</h2><p>Download the project&rsquo;s example code here: <a href=https://github.com/godotrecipes/ui_radial_menu target=_blank>https://github.com/godotrecipes/ui_radial_menu</a></p><h2 id=related-recipes>Related recipes</h2><ul><li><a href=/godot_recipes/4.x/ui/cooldown_button/>UI: Cooldown Button</a></li></ul><footer class=footline></footer>"
msgstr ""

