#: 4.x/ui/cooldown_button/index.html
msgid "<h1 id=cooldown-button>Cooldown Button</h1><h2 id=problem>Problem</h2><p>You want to make RPG-style ability buttons, including a cooldown effect.</p><p><a href=#image-1f0193be75176f946b460739a2d1c5da class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/cooldown_01.gif alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-1f0193be75176f946b460739a2d1c5da><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/cooldown_01.gif alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><h2 id=solution>Solution</h2><p>If you need art for your buttons, you can find a wide variety of well-designed buttons at <a href=https://game-icons.net/ target=_blank>Game-icons.net</a>. We&rsquo;ll be using a few from there for this recipe.</p><h3 id=node-setup>Node setup</h3><p>The scene for our ability button will need the following nodes:</p><p>Drop your chosen icon into the <strong>Textures/Normal</strong> property of the .</p><p>On the node, choose &ldquo;Full Rect&rdquo; from the <strong>Presets</strong> menu. Set the <strong>Fill Mode</strong> to &ldquo;Counter Clockwise&rdquo;.</p><p>We also want our cooldown &ldquo;radial wipe&rdquo; to darken the button, so set the <strong>Modulate</strong> property to a dark gray with some transparency:</p><p><a href=#image-4926742177212585ac6872cdf2cf6958 class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/cooldown_02.png alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-4926742177212585ac6872cdf2cf6958><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/cooldown_02.png alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><p>The <i class=gd-Timer></i> node should be set to &ldquo;One Shot&rdquo;.</p><p> is a container to hold and align the text. Set its layout to &ldquo;Bottom Wide&rdquo;, and in its <strong>Theme Overrides/Constants</strong>, both <strong>Margin Right</strong> and <strong>Margin Left</strong> to .</p><p>Finally, on the label, set <strong>Horizontal Alignment</strong> to &ldquo;Right&rdquo; and <strong>Clip Text</strong> to &ldquo;On&rdquo;. Add a font to the <strong>Theme Overrides/Font</strong>. Put a value like in the <strong>Text</strong> field to check how it works. Since our icon is black and white, it also helps to add a <strong>Theme Overrides/Constants/Outline Size</strong>_ of .</p><h3 id=script>Script</h3><p>Add a script to the . Connect the &rsquo;s signal and the &rsquo;s signal.</p><div class=highlight></div><p>We start by exporting a variable for the length of our ability&rsquo;s cooldown. Then, in the method, we can set the to use that value. Then we hide the label, because we only want to display it during the countdown.</p><p>Next, we need a texture to assign to the <i class=gd-TextureProgressBar></i> display. In this case, we&rsquo;ll copy the texture from the button - you could also use a different texture if you like.</p><p>Finally, we make sure the sweep&rsquo;s value is at , and set the node&rsquo;s processing to . We&rsquo;ll do the animation in so we don&rsquo;t need it running when we&rsquo;re not in cooldown mode.</p><div class=highlight></div><p>In we use the on the timer to set the label&rsquo;s and the sweep&rsquo;s .</p><div class=highlight></div><p>When the button is clicked, everything gets started.</p><div class=highlight></div><p>And everything is reset when the timer runs out. Put several buttons in an <i class=gd-HBoxContainer></i> and you&rsquo;ve got an action bar:</p><p><a href=#image-74ead6a5f8cb622752e6f83b3a90610c class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/cooldown_03.gif alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-74ead6a5f8cb622752e6f83b3a90610c><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/cooldown_03.gif alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><h2 id=i-classfas-fa-code-branchi-download-this-project><i class=\"fas fa-code-branch\"></i> Download This Project</h2><p>Download the project&rsquo;s example code here: <a href=https://github.com/godotrecipes/ui_cooldown_button target=_blank>https://github.com/godotrecipes/ui_cooldown_button</a></p><footer class=footline></footer>"
msgstr ""

