#: 4.x/ai/homing_missile/index.html
msgid "<h1 id=homing-missile>Homing missile</h1><h2 id=problem>Problem</h2><p>You need a &ldquo;homing missile&rdquo; - a projectile that will seek a moving target.</p><h2 id=solution>Solution</h2><p>For this example, we&rsquo;ll use an <i class=gd-Area2D></i> node for the projectile. Areas are typically good choices for bullets because we need to detect when they contact something. If you also need a bullet that bounces/ricochets, one of the type node might be a better choice.</p><p>The node setup and behavior of the missile is the same you would use for a &ldquo;dumb&rdquo; bullet. If you&rsquo;re creating many bullet types, you can use inheritance to base all your projectiles on the same core setup.</p><p>The nodes we&rsquo;ll use:</p><p>For the texture, you can use any image you like. Here&rsquo;s an example one:</p><p><a href=#image-0480bed2b6954e87c80c94b506307b4d class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/missile.png alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-0480bed2b6954e87c80c94b506307b4d><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/missile.png alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><p>Set up the nodes and configure the sprite&rsquo;s texture and the collision shape. Make sure to rotate the <i class=gd-Sprite2D></i> node by so that it&rsquo;s pointing to the right, ensuring it matches the parent&rsquo;s &ldquo;forward&rdquo; direction.</p><p>Add a script and connect the <i class=gd-Area2d></i>&rsquo;s signal and the <i class=gd-Timer></i>&rsquo;s signal.</p><p>Here&rsquo;s the starting script:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>This creates a &ldquo;dumb&rdquo; rocket that travels in a straight line when fired. To use this projectile, instance it and call its method with the desired to set its position and direction.</p><p>See the <a href=#related-recipes>related recipes</a> section below for more information.</p><p>To change the behavior to seek a target, we&rsquo;ll use the . However, we don&rsquo;t want the missile to &ldquo;turn on a dime&rdquo;, so we&rsquo;ll add a variable to control its &ldquo;steering&rdquo; force. This will give the missile a turning radius that can be adjusted for different behavior. We also need a variable so that the missile knows what to chase. We&rsquo;ll set that in as well:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>To change the missile&rsquo;s direction to move toward the target, it needs to accelerate in that direction (acceleration is change in velocity). The missile &ldquo;wants&rdquo; to move straight towards the target, but its current velocity is pointing in a different direction. Using a little vector math, we can find that difference:</p><p><a href=#image-5482f6588d79a4915f5105cb494dc4e6 class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/steering_diagram.png alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-5482f6588d79a4915f5105cb494dc4e6><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/steering_diagram.png alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><p>The green arrow represents the needed change in velocity (i.e. ). However, if we turn instantly, that will look unnatural, so the &ldquo;steering&rdquo; vector&rsquo;s length needs to be limited. This is the purpose of the variable.</p><p>This is the function to calculate that acceleration. Note that if there&rsquo;s no target, there will be no steering, so the missile remains traveling in a straight line.</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Finally, the resulting steer force must be applied in :</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Here&rsquo;s an example of the results, with a little extra visual flair such as particle smoke and explosions:</p><p><video controls src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/homing_missiles.webm></video></p><p>Here&rsquo;s the full script, including the above effects. See <a href=#related-recipes>related recipes</a> for details.</p><div class=highlight></div><h2 id=related-recipes>Related recipes</h2><ul><li><a href=/godot_recipes/4.x/animation/spritesheet_animation/>Spritesheet animation</a></li><li><a href=/godot_recipes/4.x/2d/topdown_movement/#option-2-rotate-and-move>Top-down character</a></li><li><a href=/godot_recipes/4.x/math/transforms>Transforms</a></li></ul><footer class=footline></footer>"
