#: 4.x/2d/line_collision/index.html
msgid "<h1 id=line2d-collision>Line2D Collision</h1><h2 id=problem>Problem</h2><p>You want to have collisions with a <i class=gd-Line2D></i>.</p><h2 id=solution>Solution</h2><h3 id=node-setup>Node setup</h3><p>Add the following nodes to your scene, and draw your line as desired:</p><p>Don&rsquo;t add a collision shape to the body yet!</p><div class=\"box notices cstyle note\"><div class=box-label><i class=\"fa-fw fas fa-exclamation-circle\"></i> Note</div><div class=box-content><p>You can use an <i class=gd-Area2D></i> instead if you want to detect overlap with the line rather than collision.</p></div></div><p>Next, we need to add collision shapes to the body. We have two options:</p><h3 id=option-1-using-hahahugoshortcode11s4hbhbsegmentshape2d>Option 1: Using <i class=gd-SegmentShape2D></i></h3><p><i class=gd-SegmentShape2D></i> is a line-segment collision shape. The idea here is to create a segment collision for each pair of points in the line.</p><div class=highlight></div><h3 id=option-2-using-hahahugoshortcode11s6hbhbrectangleshape2d>Option 2: Using <i class=gd-RectangleShape2D></i></h3><p><i class=gd-SegmentShape2D></i> does not have any width component, so if you need your line collision to have a thickness, you can use a rectangle collision instead.</p><div class=highlight></div><h2 id=i-classfas-fa-code-branchi-download-this-project><i class=\"fas fa-code-branch\"></i> Download This Project</h2><p>Download the project&rsquo;s example code here: <a href=https://github.com/godotrecipes/line2d_collision target=_blank>https://github.com/godotrecipes/line2d_collision</a></p><footer class=footline></footer>"
msgstr ""

