#: 4.x/2d/8_direction/index.html
msgid "<h1 id=8-directional-movementanimation>8-Directional Movement/Animation</h1><h2 id=problem>Problem</h2><p>You need a 2D character that has 8-directional movement, including animation.</p><h2 id=solution>Solution</h2><p>For our example, we&rsquo;ll use the <a href=https://remos.itch.io/mini-crusader target=_blank>Isometric Mini-Crusader</a>, which contains 8-directional animations for idle, run, attack, and several other states.</p><p><a href=#image-b324e707b17cce6f02551328c8c8a0c4 class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/8_direction_01.gif alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-b324e707b17cce6f02551328c8c8a0c4><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/8_direction_01.gif alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><p>The animations are organized in folders, with a separate image for each frame. We&rsquo;ll use an <i class=gd-AnimatedSprite2D></i> and we&rsquo;ll name each animation based on its direction. For example, pointing to the right and going clockwise to .</p><p>When our character moves, it will pick an animation based on the direction of movement:</p><p><a href=#image-8524e0c119507b60893aecf41d2dd658 class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/8_direction_03w.png alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-8524e0c119507b60893aecf41d2dd658><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/8_direction_03w.png alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><p>We&rsquo;ll use the mouse to move - the character will always face the mouse and run in that direction when we click the mouse button.</p><p>To choose which animation to play, we need to get the mouse direction and map it to this same range of . gives us the position of the mouse relative to the character. We can then use to snap the angle of the mouse vector to the closest multiple of 45° ( radians) giving the following result:</p><p><a href=#image-793c82021060162315dcb683041608fc class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/8_direction_04w.png alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-793c82021060162315dcb683041608fc><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/8_direction_04w.png alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><p>Divide each value by 45° ( radians), and we have:</p><p><a href=#image-d55ac033be87e085a198a7694ebffbd2 class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/8_direction_02w.png alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-d55ac033be87e085a198a7694ebffbd2><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/8_direction_02w.png alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><p>Finally, we need to map the resulting range to using the function, and we&rsquo;ll have our correct values. Adding that value to the end of the animation name (&ldquo;idle&rdquo;, &ldquo;run&rdquo;, etc) gives us the correct animation:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Testing the movement, we see this:</p><p><a href=#image-b9d4ed1e4f19a8329e02f55c1ef42f94 class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/8_direction_05.gif alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-b9d4ed1e4f19a8329e02f55c1ef42f94><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/8_direction_05.gif alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><h3 id=keyboard-input>Keyboard input</h3><p>If you&rsquo;re using keyboard controls instead of mouse, you can get the angle of movement based on which keys are being held. The rest of the process works in the same way.</p><div class=highlight></div><h2 id=i-classfas-fa-code-branchi-download-this-project><i class=\"fas fa-code-branch\"></i> Download This Project</h2><p>Download the project code here: <a href=https://github.com/godotrecipes/8_direction_animation target=_blank>https://github.com/godotrecipes/8_direction_animation</a></p><footer class=footline></footer>"
msgstr ""

