#: 4.x/2d/screen_wrap/index.html
msgid "<h1 id=screen-wrap>Screen wrap</h1><h2 id=problem>Problem</h2><p>You want to allow the player to &ldquo;wrap around&rdquo; the screen, teleporting from one side of the screen to the other. This is a common feature, especially in old-school 2D games (think Pac-man).</p><h2 id=solution>Solution</h2><ol><li><p>Get your screen (viewport) size</p><div class=highlight></div><p> is available to any derived node.</p></li><li><p>Compare your player&rsquo;s position</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Note that this is using the node&rsquo;s , which is usually the center of your sprite and/or body.</p></li><li><p>Simplifying with </p><p>The above code can be simplified using GDScript&rsquo;s function, which &ldquo;loops&rdquo; a value between the given limits.</p><div class=highlight></div></li></ol><footer class=footline></footer>"
msgstr ""

