#: 4.x/2d/2d_shooting/index.html
msgid "<h1 id=shooting-projectiles>Shooting projectiles</h1><h2 id=problem>Problem</h2><p>You want to shoot projectiles from your player/mob/etc..</p><h2 id=solution>Solution</h2><h3 id=setting-up-the-bullet>Setting up the bullet</h3><p>First, we&rsquo;ll set up a &ldquo;bullet&rdquo; object that we can instance. Here are the nodes we&rsquo;ll use:</p><p>For the <i class=gd-Sprite2D></i>&rsquo;s texture, you can use any image you like. Here&rsquo;s an example one:</p><p><a href=#image-ea02bb0f6e212ea8f89ac0e9a4376ab3 class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/laserRed01.png alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-ea02bb0f6e212ea8f89ac0e9a4376ab3><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/laserRed01.png alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><p>Set up the nodes and configure the sprite and collision shape. If your texture is oriented pointing up, like the one above, make sure to rotate the <i class=gd-Sprite2D></i> node by so that it&rsquo;s pointing to the right, ensuring it matches the parent’s “forward” direction.</p><p>Add a script and connect the <i class=gd-Area2D></i>&rsquo;s signal.</p><div class=highlight></div><p>For this example, we&rsquo;ll remove the bullet if it hits anything at all. We&rsquo;ll also delete anything tagged in the &ldquo;mobs&rdquo; group that it hits.</p><h3 id=shooting>Shooting</h3><p>We need to set up a spawn location for the bullets. Add a <i class=gd-Marker2D></i> and place it where you want the bullets to spawn. Here&rsquo;s an example, placed at the barrel of the gun. I&rsquo;ve named it &ldquo;Muzzle&rdquo;.</p><p><a href=#image-2e3b15b357b88a94c4d0e736ea817ff5 class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/2d_shoot_01.gif alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-2e3b15b357b88a94c4d0e736ea817ff5><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/2d_shoot_01.gif alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><p>Notice that as the player rotates, the Muzzle&rsquo;s remains oriented the same way relative to the gun. This will be very convenient when spawning the bullets, as they can use the transform to get the proper position <em>and</em> direction. We just set the new bullet&rsquo;s equal to the muzzle&rsquo;s.</p><div class=\"box notices cstyle tip\"><div class=box-label><i class=\"fa-fw fas fa-lightbulb\"></i> Tip</div><div class=box-content><p>This will work for any character type, not just the &ldquo;rotate-and-move&rdquo; style shown here. Just attach the <i class=gd-Marker2D></i> where you want the bullets to spawn.</p></div></div><p>In the character&rsquo;s script we add a variable to hold the bullet scene for instancing:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>And check for our defined input action:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Now in our function we can instance a bullet and add it to the tree. A common mistake is to add the bullet as a child of the player:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>The problem here is that since the bullets are children of the player, they are affected when the player moves or rotates.</p><p><a href=#image-0c1292ff189570a5e5e4b2a1140f8587 class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/2d_shoot_02.gif alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-0c1292ff189570a5e5e4b2a1140f8587><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/2d_shoot_02.gif alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><p>To fix this, we should make sure the bullets are added to the world instead. In this case, we&rsquo;ll use , which refers to the root node of the scene the player is in. Note that we also need to use the muzzle&rsquo;s <em>global</em> transform, or else the bullet would not be where we expected.</p><div class=highlight></div><p><a href=#image-30350521631126f55411e8498fb400c2 class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/2d_shoot_03.gif alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-30350521631126f55411e8498fb400c2><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/2d_shoot_03.gif alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><h2 id=related-recipes>Related recipes</h2><ul><li><a href=/godot_recipes/4.x/math/transforms/>Gamedev Math: transforms</a></li></ul><h2 id=i-classfas-fa-code-branchi-download-this-project><i class=\"fas fa-code-branch\"></i> Download This Project</h2><p>Download the project code here: <a href=https://github.com/godotrecipes/2d_shooting target=_blank>https://github.com/godotrecipes/2d_shooting</a></p><footer class=footline></footer>"
msgstr ""

