#: 4.x/2d/topdown_movement/index.html
msgid "<h1 id=top-down-movement>Top-down movement</h1><h2 id=problem>Problem</h2><p>You&rsquo;re making a 2D top-down game, and you want to control a character&rsquo;s movement.</p><h2 id=solution>Solution</h2><p>For this solution, we&rsquo;ll assume you have the following input actions defined:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Action Name</th><th>Key(s)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td>W,↑</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>S,↓</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>D,→</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>A,←</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Mouse button 1</td></tr></tbody></table><p>We will also assume you&rsquo;re using a <i class=gd-CharacterBody2D></i> node.</p><p>We can solve this problem in many ways, depending on what type of behavior you&rsquo;re looking for.</p><h3 id=option-1-8-way-movement>Option 1: 8-way movement</h3><p>In this scenario, the player uses the four directional keys to move (including diagonals).</p><div class=highlight></div><h3 id=option-2-rotate-and-move>Option 2: Rotate and move</h3><p>In this scenario, the left/right actions rotate the character and up/down move the character forward and back in whatever direction it&rsquo;s facing. This is sometimes referred to as &ldquo;Asteroids-style&rdquo; movement.</p><div class=highlight></div><div class=\"box notices cstyle note\"><div class=box-label><i class=\"fa-fw fas fa-exclamation-circle\"></i> Note</div><div class=box-content><p>Godot considers an angle of degrees to be pointing along the axis. This means that a node&rsquo;s forward direction () is to the right. You should ensure that your character&rsquo;s sprite is also drawn pointing to the right.</p></div></div><h3 id=option-3-aim-with-mouse>Option 3: Aim with mouse</h3><p>Similar to option 2, but this time the character rotation is controlled with the mouse (ie the character always points towards the mouse). Forward/back movement is done with the keys as before.</p><div class=highlight></div><h3 id=option-4-click-and-move>Option 4: Click and move</h3><p>In this option, the character moves to the clicked location.</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Note that we stop moving if we get close to the target position. If you don&rsquo;t do this, the character will &ldquo;jiggle&rdquo; back and forth as it moves a little bit past the target, moves back, goes a little past it, and so on. Optionally, you can use to face in the direction of movement.</p><h2 id=i-classfas-fa-code-branchi-download-this-project><i class=\"fas fa-code-branch\"></i> Download This Project</h2><p>Download the project code here: <a href=https://github.com/godotrecipes/topdown_movement target=_blank>https://github.com/godotrecipes/topdown_movement</a></p><footer class=footline></footer>"
msgstr ""

