#: 4.x/2d/multi_target_camera/index.html
msgid "<h1 id=multitarget-camera>Multitarget Camera</h1><h2 id=problem>Problem</h2><p>You need a dynamic camera that moves and zooms to keep multiple objects on screen at the same time.</p><p>An example might be in a 2 player game, keeping both players on-screen as they move farther and closer together, like so:</p><p><a href=#image-e5900f5b4a6b1668caf6b7d19d1413ac class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/multi_cam_01.gif alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-e5900f5b4a6b1668caf6b7d19d1413ac><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/multi_cam_01.gif alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><h2 id=solution>Solution</h2><p>In a single-player game, you&rsquo;re probably used to attaching the camera to the player, so that it automatically follows them. We can&rsquo;t really do this here because we have 2 (or more) players or other game objects that we want to keep on the screen at all times.</p><p>We need our camera to do 3 things:</p><ol><li>Add/remove any number of targets.</li><li>Keep the camera&rsquo;s position centered at the midpoint of the targets.</li><li>Adjust the camera&rsquo;s zoom to keep all targets on screen.</li></ol><p>Create a new scene with a <i class=gd-Camera2D></i> and attach a script. We&rsquo;ll add this camera to our game once we&rsquo;re done.</p><p>Let&rsquo;s break down how the script works.</p><div class=\"box notices cstyle note\"><div class=box-label><i class=\"fa-fw fas fa-exclamation-circle\"></i> Note</div><div class=box-content><p>You can see the full script at the <a href=#full-script>end of the article</a>.</p></div></div><p>Here&rsquo;s how the script starts:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>These settings will let you adjust the camera&rsquo;s behavior. We&rsquo;ll all camera changes, so setting the move/zoom speeds to lower values will introduce some delay in the camera &ldquo;catching up&rdquo; to sudden changes.</p><p>Maximum and minimum zoom values will also depend on the size of objects in your game and how close or far you want to get. Adjust to suit.</p><p>The property is going to add some extra space around the targets so they&rsquo;re not right on the edge of the viewable area.</p><p>Lastly, we have our array of targets and we get the viewport size so that we can properly calculate the scale.</p><div class=highlight></div><p>For adding and removing targets, we have two helper functions. You can use these during gameplay to change what targets are being tracked (&ldquo;Player 3 has entered the game!&rdquo;). Note that we don&rsquo;t want to have the same target tracked twice, so we reject it if it&rsquo;s already there.</p><p>Most of the functionality happens in . First, moving the camera:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Here, we loop through the targets&rsquo; positions and find the common center. Using we make sure it moves there smoothly.</p><p>Next, we&rsquo;ll handle the zoom:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>The key functionality here comes from . We want to find a rectangle that encloses all the targets, which we can get with the method. We then grow the rect by the .</p><p>Here you can see the rectangle being drawn (press &ldquo;Tab&rdquo; in the demo project to enable this drawing):</p><p><a href=#image-e8b98d870f7d303f95ba1b26292f4172 class=lightbox-link><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/multi_cam_02.gif alt=alt style=height:auto;width:auto loading=lazy> </a><a href=javascript:history.back(); class=lightbox id=image-e8b98d870f7d303f95ba1b26292f4172><img src=/godot_recipes/4.x/img/multi_cam_02.gif alt=alt class=lightbox-image loading=lazy></a></p><p>Then, depending whether the rectangle is wider or taller (relative to the screen&rsquo;s aspect ratio), we find the scale and clamp it in the max/min range we&rsquo;ve defined.</p><h2 id=full-script>Full script</h2><div class=highlight></div><h2 id=i-classfas-fa-code-branchi-download-this-project><i class=\"fas fa-code-branch\"></i> Download This Project</h2><p>Download the project&rsquo;s example code here: <a href=https://github.com/godotrecipes/multitarget_camera target=_blank>https://github.com/godotrecipes/multitarget_camera</a></p><footer class=footline></footer>"
msgstr ""

