#: 4.x/games/first_2d/first_2d_10/index.html
msgid "<h1 id=starting-and-ending-the-game>Starting and Ending the Game</h1><p>Our last step is to add a start button and a &ldquo;game over&rdquo; state to the game.</p><h2 id=starting-the-game>Starting the game</h2><p>Currently when we run the game, it starts immediately. Let&rsquo;s add a button to start it.</p><p>In as a child of the , add a <i class=gd-CenterContainer></i> and set its layout to <strong>Full Rect</strong>. Then add a <i class=gd-TextureButton></i> child. Name this button and add the image as its <strong>Normal</strong> texture.</p><p>Add a reference at the top of the script:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Connect this button&rsquo;s texture to and add this code:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>The function handles starting the game, so change so that it no longer spawns enemies, but just ensures the button is showing:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Now add the function:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Now the button should show when you run the scene, and pressing it starts the game.</p><h2 id=ending-the-game>Ending the game</h2><p>Add a <i class=gd-TextureRect></i> as a child of the and name the node . Use the image. It will overlap with the start button, but that&rsquo;s ok, we&rsquo;re only ever going to show one at a time.</p><p>Add another reference at the top of the script:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>And add to .</p><p>Connect the player&rsquo;s signal in .</p><div class=highlight></div><p>This will show the &ldquo;game over&rdquo; image for 2 seconds, then switch back to the start button so you can play again. Try it out and see if you can play a few games.</p><table><thead><tr><th><span class=\"btn cstyle transparent\"><a href=/godot_recipes/4.x/games/first_2d/first_2d_09/><i class=\"fas fa-arrow-left\"></i> Prev</a></span></th><th style=text-align:right><span class=\"btn cstyle transparent\"><a href=/godot_recipes/4.x/games/first_2d/first_2d_end/>Next <i class=\"fas fa-arrow-right\"></i></a></span></th></tr></thead></table><footer class=footline></footer>"
