#: 4.x/games/first_2d/first_2d_08/index.html
msgid "<h1 id=enemy-shooting>Enemy Shooting</h1><p>Now that our enemy can shoot, let&rsquo;s give them something to shoot at.</p><h2 id=enemy-bullet-scene>Enemy bullet scene</h2><p>Make a new scene just like you made the player bullet earlier. We won&rsquo;t go into all the steps here, but you can refer back to that part if you&rsquo;re stuck. The only difference here is that you can use the image instead.</p><p>The script will be a little bit different:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Connect the and signals of the <i class=gd-VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D></i> and <i class=gd-Area2D></i>, respectively:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Notice that we&rsquo;re detecting the hit on the player, but it&rsquo;s not doing anything yet. We&rsquo;ll come back to that once we add a way for the player to take damage.</p><h2 id=adding-shooting-to-the-enemy>Adding shooting to the enemy</h2><p>At the top of the enemy&rsquo;s script, load the new bullet:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Then update the shooting function:</p><div class=highlight></div><p>Play the scene again and you should have some random enemy bullets appearing.</p><table><thead><tr><th><span class=\"btn cstyle transparent\"><a href=/godot_recipes/4.x/games/first_2d/first_2d_07/><i class=\"fas fa-arrow-left\"></i> Prev</a></span></th><th style=text-align:right><span class=\"btn cstyle transparent\"><a href=/godot_recipes/4.x/games/first_2d/first_2d_09/>Next <i class=\"fas fa-arrow-right\"></i></a></span></th></tr></thead></table><footer class=footline></footer>"
msgstr ""

